/-!
# The join of two finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of an algebra on an algebraic space

Let `F` be an algebraic space and `A` a sheaf of commutative `𝒪_F`-algebras on its small étale
site.  Given morphisms `c : C ⟶ A` and `d : D ⟶ A` of algebra sheaves, this file constructs the
subsheaf of rings of `A` generated by the images of `C` and of `D`, namely the sheafification of
the subpresheaf of rings whose sections over a chart are the subring generated by the images of
the sections of `C` and of `D`.

Over an *affine* étale chart the sections of the generated subalgebra are exactly the subring
generated by the images of the sections there — no sheafification is seen — and from this both
its quasi-coherence and its finite type follow.  Consequently any two finite type quasi-coherent
subalgebras of a quasi-coherent `A` are contained in a third, so the finite type quasi-coherent
subalgebras of `A` form a filtered category.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.generatedRingSubpresheaf`: the subpresheaf of rings of
  `A` generated by the images of `C` and of `D`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.join`: its sheafification, as an algebra sheaf, with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.joinι` its inclusion into `A` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.joinInl`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.joinInr` the factorisations of `c` and of `d` through it.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.mem_joinSubpresheaf_iff_mem_span`: over an affine étale
  chart the sections of the join are the `𝒪_F`-span of the products of sections of `C` and `D`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.isQuasicoherent_join` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.isFiniteType_join`: **the join of two quasi-coherent
  algebras is quasi-coherent, and of finite type as soon as both are.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_dominating` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra`: **the finite type quasi-coherent
  subalgebras of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf are filtered**, with no quasi-compactness or
  quasi-separatedness hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

The sheaf condition for the generated subsheaf of rings is not Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_forget`, which asks the coefficient category to have
limits of the size of the site; it is
`Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_commRingCat_of_isSheaf_forget'` applied to
`Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.sheafify_isSheaf`, the sheaf condition of the underlying
subpresheaf of types.

Quasi-coherence is read off through cartesianness on affine charts: injectivity of the base
change comparison comes from the inclusion into `A` together with flatness of the restriction map
of regular functions between affine charts, and surjectivity from the description of the sections
over an affine chart as a span of products, each product over the smaller chart being a
combination of restrictions of products over the larger one.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 082B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/082B)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace RingHom

/-- The image of any element under an algebra map from an algebra generated by `s` lies in the
adjoin of any set containing the image of `s`. -/
private theorem mem_adjoin_of_adjoin_eq_top {R X T : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing X]
    [CommRing T] [Algebra R X] [Algebra R T] (f : X →ₐ[R] T) {s : Finset X}
    (hs : Algebra.adjoin R (s : Set X) = ⊤) (x : X) {U : Set T} (hU : f '' s ⊆ U) :
    f x ∈ Algebra.adjoin R U := by
  have hx : f x ∈ (Algebra.adjoin R (s : Set X)).map f :=
    Subalgebra.mem_map.2 ⟨x, by rw [hs]; exact Algebra.mem_top, rfl⟩
  rw [AlgHom.map_adjoin] at hx
  exact Algebra.adjoin_mono hU hx

/-- **A subring generated by the images of two finite type algebras is of finite type.**

Let `γ : Cc →+* Aa` and `δ : Dd →+* Aa` take their values in a subring `T` of `Aa`, let `ρ` be
the induced map `R →+* T`, and let `Cc` and `Dd` be of finite type over `R` compatibly with `γ`
and `δ`.  If `T` is contained in the subring of `Aa` generated by the images of `γ` and of `δ`,
then `T` is of finite type over `R`: the images of finite generating families of `Cc` and of `Dd`
generate it. -/
theorem finiteType_of_closure_range_union {R Cc Dd Aa : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing Cc]
    [CommRing Dd] [CommRing Aa] (T : Subring Aa) (γ : Cc →+* Aa) (δ : Dd →+* Aa)
    (ρc : R →+* Cc) (ρd : R →+* Dd) (ρ : R →+* T)
    (hγ : ∀ x, γ x ∈ T) (hδ : ∀ x, δ x ∈ T)
    (hργ : ∀ r, ((ρ r : Aa)) = γ (ρc r)) (hρδ : ∀ r, ((ρ r : Aa)) = δ (ρd r))
    (hC : ρc.FiniteType) (hD : ρd.FiniteType)
    (hT : ∀ y : T, (y : Aa) ∈ Subring.closure (Set.range γ ∪ Set.range δ)) :
    ρ.FiniteType := by
  classical
  let _ : Algebra R Cc := ρc.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra R Dd := ρd.toAlgebra
  let _ : Algebra R T := ρ.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (hC : Algebra.FiniteType R Cc).out
  obtain ⟨t, ht⟩ := (hD : Algebra.FiniteType R Dd).out
  let γ' : Cc →ₐ[R] T :=
    { toRingHom := γ.codRestrict T hγ
      commutes' := fun r => Subtype.ext (hργ r).symm }
  let δ' : Dd →ₐ[R] T :=
    { toRingHom := δ.codRestrict T hδ
      commutes' := fun r => Subtype.ext (hρδ r).symm }
  refine ⟨⟨s.image γ' ∪ t.image δ', le_antisymm le_top fun y _ => ?_⟩⟩
  have hgen : Subring.closure (Set.range γ ∪ Set.range δ) ≤
      Subring.map T.subtype
        (Algebra.adjoin R (↑(s.image γ' ∪ t.image δ') : Set T)).toSubring := by
    refine Subring.closure_le.2 ?_
    rintro v (⟨x, rfl⟩ | ⟨x, rfl⟩)
    · exact Subring.mem_map.2 ⟨γ' x, mem_adjoin_of_adjoin_eq_top γ' hs x (by
        rw [← Finset.coe_image]; exact_mod_cast Finset.subset_union_left), rfl⟩
    · exact Subring.mem_map.2 ⟨δ' x, mem_adjoin_of_adjoin_eq_top δ' ht x (by
        rw [← Finset.coe_image]; exact_mod_cast Finset.subset_union_right), rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hwy⟩ := Subring.mem_map.1 (hgen (hT y))
  have hwy' : w = y := Subtype.ext hwy
  rw [← hwy']
  exact hw

end RingHom

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F)

/-! ### A jointly faithfully flat finite affine family inside a covering sieve -/

variable {B S hS F hF}

namespace AlgebraSheaf

variable {A C D : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF}

/-! ### The subpresheaf of rings generated by the images of two algebras -/

/-- The subpresheaf of rings of `A` whose sections over an étale chart are the subring generated
by the images of the sections of `C` and of `D` there. -/
def generatedRingSubpresheaf (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) :
    Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf A.right.obj where
  obj V := Subring.closure (Set.range (fun x : C.right.obj.obj V => c.right.hom.app V x) ∪
    Set.range fun x : D.right.obj.obj V => d.right.hom.app V x)
  map {U V} i x hx := by
    have h : (A.right.obj.map i).hom x ∈ Subring.closure ((A.right.obj.map i).hom ''
        (Set.range (fun y : C.right.obj.obj U => c.right.hom.app U y) ∪
          Set.range fun y : D.right.obj.obj U => d.right.hom.app U y)) := by
      rw [← RingHom.map_closure]
      exact Subring.mem_map.2 ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    refine Subring.closure_le.2 ?_ h
    rintro y ⟨w, (⟨z, rfl⟩ | ⟨z, rfl⟩), rfl⟩
    · exact Subring.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨C.right.obj.map i z, app_map c i z⟩)
    · exact Subring.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨D.right.obj.map i z, app_map d i z⟩)

/-! ### The generated subsheaf of rings, as an algebra sheaf -/

/-- The subsheaf of rings of `A` generated by the images of `C` and of `D`: the sheafification of
the subpresheaf of rings they generate, so its sections over a chart are the sections of `A`
which lie in that subring locally on the chart. -/
def joinSubpresheaf (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) :
    Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf A.right.obj :=
  (generatedRingSubpresheaf c d).sheafify (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F)

/-- A section of `A` lying in the subring generated by the images of the sections of `C` and of
`D` lies in the generated subsheaf of rings. -/
theorem mem_joinSubpresheaf_of_mem_closure (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A)
    {V : (SmallEtale B S hS F)ᵒᵖ} {y : A.right.obj.obj V}
    (hy : y ∈ Subring.closure (Set.range (fun x : C.right.obj.obj V => c.right.hom.app V x) ∪
      Set.range fun x : D.right.obj.obj V => d.right.hom.app V x)) :
    y ∈ (joinSubpresheaf c d).obj V :=
  Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.le_sheafify _ _ V hy

/-- The image of a section of `C` lies in the subsheaf of rings generated by the images of `C`
and of `D`. -/
theorem app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_left (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (V : (SmallEtale B S hS F)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : C.right.obj.obj V) : c.right.hom.app V x ∈ (joinSubpresheaf c d).obj V :=
  mem_joinSubpresheaf_of_mem_closure c d (Subring.subset_closure (Or.inl ⟨x, rfl⟩))

/-- The image of a section of `D` lies in the subsheaf of rings generated by the images of `C`
and of `D`. -/
theorem app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_right (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (V : (SmallEtale B S hS F)ᵒᵖ)
    (x : D.right.obj.obj V) : d.right.hom.app V x ∈ (joinSubpresheaf c d).obj V :=
  mem_joinSubpresheaf_of_mem_closure c d (Subring.subset_closure (Or.inr ⟨x, rfl⟩))

/-- The presheaf of rings of sections of the subsheaf generated by the images of `C` and of `D`
is a sheaf: in types it is the sheafification of a subpresheaf of the sheaf of all sections of
`A`. -/
theorem isSheaf_joinSubpresheaf_toPresheaf (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F) (joinSubpresheaf c d).toPresheaf := by
  refine Stacks.Sites.isSheaf_commRingCat_of_isSheaf_forget' _ _ ?_
  refine Presieve.isSheaf_iso _ (joinSubpresheaf c d).forgetIso.symm ?_
  exact Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.sheafify_isSheaf
    (G := generatedRingSubpresheaf c d) (isSheaf_sectionsPresheaf A)

/-- **The subalgebra of `A` generated by the images of `C` and of `D`.**  Its sections over a
chart are the sections of `A` which locally lie in the subring generated by the images of the
sections of `C` and of `D`; the structure-algebra map of `A` lands there because it factors
through `c`. -/
def join (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF where
  right := ⟨(joinSubpresheaf c d).toPresheaf, isSheaf_joinSubpresheaf_toPresheaf c d⟩
  algebraMap V :=
    (A.algebraMap V).codRestrict ((joinSubpresheaf c d).obj V) fun r => by
      rw [← c.comm V r]
      exact app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_left c d V (C.algebraMap V r)
  algebraMap_natural f r := Subtype.ext (A.algebraMap_natural f r)

/-- The inclusion of the subalgebra generated by the images of `C` and of `D` into `A`. -/
def joinι (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : join c d ⟶ A where
  right := ObjectProperty.homMk (joinSubpresheaf c d).ι
  comm _ _ := rfl

/-- The inclusion of the generated subalgebra is injective on the sections over every chart. -/
theorem joinι_app_injective (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (V : (SmallEtale B S hS F)ᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Injective (((joinι c d).right.hom.app V).hom) :=
  Subtype.val_injective

/-- The inclusion of the generated subalgebra is a monomorphism of the underlying sheaves of
commutative rings: it is injective on sections, and the embedding of sheaves into presheaves
reflects monomorphisms. -/
instance mono_joinι_right (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : Mono (joinι c d).right := by
  have : ∀ V : (SmallEtale B S hS F)ᵒᵖ, Mono ((joinι c d).right.hom.app V) := fun V =>
    ConcreteCategory.mono_of_injective _ (joinι_app_injective c d V)
  exact (sheafToPresheaf (SmallEtale.topology B S hS F) CommRingCat.{u}).mono_of_mono_map
    (NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app (joinι c d).right.hom)

/-- The inclusion of the generated subalgebra is a monomorphism of algebra sheaves: forgetting
the algebra structure is faithful, so it reflects monomorphisms. -/
instance mono_joinι (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : Mono (joinι c d) :=
  Functor.mono_of_mono_map (forget (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (F := F) (hF := hF))
    (mono_joinι_right c d)

/-- The factorisation of `c` through the subalgebra generated by the images of `C` and of `D`. -/
def joinInl (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : C ⟶ join c d where
  right := ObjectProperty.homMk
    (Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.lift c.right.hom (app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_left c d))
  comm V r := Subtype.ext (c.comm V r)

/-- The factorisation of `d` through the subalgebra generated by the images of `C` and of `D`. -/
def joinInr (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : D ⟶ join c d where
  right := ObjectProperty.homMk
    (Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.lift d.right.hom (app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_right c d))
  comm V r := Subtype.ext (d.comm V r)

/-- The factorisation of `c` through the generated subalgebra recovers `c`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem joinInl_joinι (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : joinInl c d ≫ joinι c d = c :=
  Hom.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.lift_ι _ _))

/-- The factorisation of `d` through the generated subalgebra recovers `d`. -/
@[reassoc]
theorem joinInr_joinι (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) : joinInr c d ≫ joinι c d = d :=
  Hom.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ (Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.lift_ι _ _))

/-! ### The sections of the join over an affine chart -/

/-- **Over an affine étale chart the sections of the subalgebra generated by the images of `C`
and of `D` are exactly the `𝒪_F`-span of the products of a section of `C` and a section of
`D`**, so the sheafification is invisible there.

One inclusion is that the span is the generated subring, which the generated subpresheaf already
contains.  The other is faithfully flat descent: a covering sieve of an affine chart contains a
finite jointly faithfully flat family of affine charts, and membership in the span descends along
such a family. -/
theorem mem_joinSubpresheaf_iff_mem_span (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hD : D.IsQuasicoherent) {W : SmallEtale B S hS F}
    (hW : IsAffine ((SmallEtale.toOver B S hS F ⋙ BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj W))
    (y : A.right.obj.obj (op W)) :
    y ∈ (joinSubpresheaf c d).obj (op W) ↔
      y ∈ Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF W) (productSet c d W) := by
  constructor
  · intro hy
    rw [joinSubpresheaf, Stacks.CategoryTheory.RingSubpresheaf.mem_sheafify_iff] at hy
    obtain ⟨n, z, φ, hzaff, hzT, hff⟩ :=
      exists_finite_affine_faithfullyFlat_pi_le B S hS F hF hW hy
    refine mem_span_productSet_of_forall_restrict_of_isQuasicoherent c d hA hC hD hW φ hzaff hff
      fun i => ?_
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, span_productSet_eq_closure c d (z i)]
    exact hzT i
  · intro hy
    refine mem_joinSubpresheaf_of_mem_closure c d ?_
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, ← span_productSet_eq_closure c d W]
    exact hy

/-! ### Quasi-coherence of the join -/

/-- **The subalgebra generated by the images of two quasi-coherent algebras is cartesian on
affine charts.**

Injectivity of the base change comparison needs only the inclusion into `A`, which is injective
on sections, together with flatness of the restriction map of regular functions between affine
charts.  Surjectivity is the description of the sections over an affine chart as a span of
products: every product over the smaller chart is a combination of restrictions of products over
the larger one, and the restriction of a product over the larger chart is in the range of the
comparison. -/
theorem isCartesianOnAffineCharts_join (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hD : D.IsQuasicoherent) :
    IsCartesianOnAffineCharts (join c d).underlyingModule := by
  have hAcart := isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF _ hA
  have hCcart := isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF _ hC
  have hDcart := isCartesianOnAffineCharts_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite B S hS F hF _ hD
  intro U V hU hV f
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · refine injective_sectionsBaseChange_of_injective_app (underlyingModuleMap (joinι c d)) f
      (flat_chartRestrict_of_isAffine f hU hV) ?_ (hAcart U V hU hV f)
    intro a b h
    exact Subtype.ext h
  · intro y
    let _ := chartAlgebra (hF := hF) f
    let incl : (join c d).underlyingModule.val.obj (op V) →ₗ[chartRing B S hS F hF V]
        A.right.obj.obj (op V) := ((underlyingModuleMap (joinι c d)).val.app (op V)).hom
    have key : Submodule.span (chartRing B S hS F hF V) (productSet c d V) ≤
        Submodule.map incl
          (LinearMap.range (sectionsBaseChange (join c d).underlyingModule f)) := by
      refine Submodule.span_le.2 fun w hw => ?_
      refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
        (productSet_restrict_subset_span c d hCcart hDcart hU hV f hw)
      rintro v ⟨t, ht, rfl⟩
      have htmem : t ∈ (joinSubpresheaf c d).obj (op U) :=
        (mem_joinSubpresheaf_iff_mem_span c d hA hC hD hU t).2 (Submodule.subset_span ht)
      refine Submodule.mem_map.2 ⟨sectionsBaseChange (join c d).underlyingModule f
        (TensorProduct.tmul _ (1 : chartRing B S hS F hF V) ⟨t, htmem⟩),
        LinearMap.mem_range_self _ _, ?_⟩
      exact congrArg (fun z => incl z)
        (chartBaseChange_one_tmul (join c d).underlyingModule f ⟨t, htmem⟩)
    obtain ⟨w, hw, hwy⟩ := Submodule.mem_map.1
      (key ((mem_joinSubpresheaf_iff_mem_span c d hA hC hD hV y.1).1 y.2))
    obtain ⟨p, hp⟩ := hw
    exact ⟨p, hp.trans (Subtype.ext hwy)⟩

/-- **The subalgebra of a quasi-coherent algebra generated by the images of two quasi-coherent
algebras is quasi-coherent.**  Quasi-coherence on the small étale site of an algebraic space is
cartesianness on affine charts, Descent, Proposition 03DX(2). -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_join (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hD : D.IsQuasicoherent) : (join c d).IsQuasicoherent :=
  isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isCartesianOnAffineCharts _
    (isCartesianOnAffineCharts_join c d hA hC hD)

/-! ### Finite type of the join -/

/-- **The subalgebra generated by the images of two finite type quasi-coherent algebras is of
finite type.**

Over an affine étale chart its sections are the subring generated by the images of the sections
of `C` and of `D`, so the images of finite generating families of those two sections generate it
as an algebra over the regular functions on the chart. -/
theorem isFiniteType_join (c : C ⟶ A) (d : D ⟶ A) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent)
    (hC : C.IsQuasicoherent) (hD : D.IsQuasicoherent) (hCft : C.IsFiniteType)
    (hDft : D.IsFiniteType) : (join c d).IsFiniteType := fun W hW =>
  RingHom.finiteType_of_closure_range_union ((joinSubpresheaf c d).obj (op W))
    ((c.right.hom.app (op W)).hom) ((d.right.hom.app (op W)).hom)
    (C.algebraMap (op W)) (D.algebraMap (op W)) ((join c d).algebraMap (op W))
    (app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_left c d (op W)) (app_mem_joinSubpresheaf_right c d (op W))
    (fun r => (c.comm (op W) r).symm) (fun r => (d.comm (op W) r).symm)
    (hCft W hW) (hDft W hW) fun y => by
      rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, ← span_productSet_eq_closure c d W]
      exact (mem_joinSubpresheaf_iff_mem_span c d hA hC hD hW y.1).1 y.2

end AlgebraSheaf

/-! ### Directedness of the finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras -/

/-- **Any two finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of a quasi-coherent algebra sheaf are
contained in a third**, with no quasi-compactness or quasi-separatedness hypothesis.

The upper bound is the subalgebra generated by the images of the two, which is quasi-coherent and
of finite type, and which both of them map into over `A`. -/
theorem exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_dominating (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS F hF)
    (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent) (E₁ E₂ : FiniteTypeSubalgebra B S hS F hF A) :
    ∃ (E : FiniteTypeSubalgebra B S hS F hF A) (_ : E₁ ⟶ E) (_ : E₂ ⟶ E), True := by
  have hqc := AlgebraSheaf.isQuasicoherent_join E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow hA
    E₁.property.1 E₂.property.1
  have hft := AlgebraSheaf.isFiniteType_join E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow hA
    E₁.property.1 E₂.property.1 E₁.property.2 E₂.property.2
  refine ⟨⟨Subobject.mk (AlgebraSheaf.joinι E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow),
    AlgebraSheaf.IsQuasicoherent.of_iso
      (Subobject.underlyingIso (AlgebraSheaf.joinι E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow)).symm hqc,
    AlgebraSheaf.IsFiniteType.of_iso
      (Subobject.underlyingIso (AlgebraSheaf.joinι E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow)).symm hft⟩,
    ObjectProperty.homMk (homOfLE (Subobject.le_mk_of_comm
      (AlgebraSheaf.joinInl E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow)
      (AlgebraSheaf.joinInl_joinι _ _))),
    ObjectProperty.homMk (homOfLE (Subobject.le_mk_of_comm
      (AlgebraSheaf.joinInr E₁.obj.arrow E₂.obj.arrow)
      (AlgebraSheaf.joinInr_joinι _ _))), trivial⟩

/-- **The finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of a quasi-coherent sheaf of `𝒪_Y`-algebras on
an algebraic space form a filtered category**, with no hypothesis beyond quasi-coherence of the
algebra.

Nonemptiness is the image of the canonical morphism from the structure sheaf, and upper bounds
are the subalgebras generated by two subalgebras. -/
@[stacks 082B "the directedness assertion; the colimit assertion is blocked on Stacks 07SU
through 0829 and 07V9 by the source's own route"]
theorem isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra (Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS Y.1 Y.2) (hA : A.IsQuasicoherent) :
    IsFiltered (FiniteTypeSubalgebra B S hS Y.1 Y.2 A) :=
  isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra_of_exists_sup B S hS Y A hA
    (exists_finiteTypeSubalgebra_dominating A hA)

/-- **The finite type quasi-coherent subalgebras of the integral closure of `𝒪_Y` in itself form
a filtered category**, with no hypothesis at all.

An instance of the directedness assertion at a concrete quasi-coherent algebra sheaf: the
integral closure of the structure sheaf in a quasi-coherent algebra is quasi-coherent, and `𝒪_Y`
read as an algebra over itself is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra_integralClosureSheaf_unitAlgebra
    (Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS) :
    IsFiltered (FiniteTypeSubalgebra B S hS Y.1 Y.2
      (AlgebraSheaf.integralClosureSheaf (unitAlgebra B S hS Y))) :=
  isFiltered_finiteTypeSubalgebra Y _
    (AlgebraSheaf.isQuasicoherent_integralClosureSheaf _ (isQuasicoherent_unitAlgebra B S hS Y))

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

